<%# One act in the Operate zone: a plain sentence saying why you would (or would not)
    run it, and a button named for the command it sends — mono and lowercase, because
    it *is* the command. The full line, flags and all, is in the preview and on the
    record entry. With nothing to do the button still shows, inert, so the zone reads
    the same whatever the box's state. Locals: verb, state, button (nil when there is
    nothing to do), danger (optional). %>
<div class="act<%= ' act-danger' if local_assigns[:danger] %>">
  <span class="act-state"><%= state %></span>
  <div class="act-button">
    <%= button || tag.span(vilice_verb(verb), class: "btn cmd sm", "aria-disabled": "true", title: "Nothing to do right now") %>
  </div>
</div>
